{"_id":"68a736178ec3d8323af1635b","nodeId":"oyqw4tr-taZcxt5kREh1g","roadmapSlug":"docker","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:03.460Z","description":"# Continuous Integration (CI)\n\nContinuous integration is the idea of executing some actions (for example build, test, etc...) automatically as you push code to your version control system.\n\nFor containers, there are a number of things we may want to do:\n\n*   Build the container images\n*   Execute tests\n*   Scan container images for vulnerabilities\n*   Tag images with useful metadata\n*   Push to a container registry","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Continuous Integration - Docker","url":"https://courses.devopsdirective.com/docker-beginner-to-pro/lessons/11-development-workflow/04-continuous-integration-github-actions","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbaf0"},{"type":"feed","title":"Explore top posts about CI/CD","url":"https://app.daily.dev/tags/cicd?ref=roadmapsh","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbaf1"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-30T07:56:48.897Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416d80","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Docker","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/zzDy1W"},{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416df4","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbEdZ2"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/docker/content/oyqw4tr-taZcxt5kREh1g.md"}